================================================================================
## Add isolated multi-backend simulation sandboxes
================================================================================

Context: What-if simulations must preserve their copy-on-write and Explorer
semantics when a domain uses Lakehouse Delta or Neo4j rather than Lakebase.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/simulation/Simulation.py
   Enable simulation capability checks and Explorer relation resolution for
   Lakebase, Lakehouse Delta, and Neo4j.
2. src/back/objects/simulation/SimulationSandbox.py
   Add Delta-table and Neo4j marker-graph sandboxes, including Delta
   predicate-overlay views and lifecycle cleanup.
3. src/back/core/reasoning/swrl/SWRLFlatCypherTranslator.py
   Translate class and object-property SWRL rules to read-only Neo4j Cypher
   and reject unsupported atoms explicitly.
4. src/back/core/graphdb/neo4j/Neo4jStore.py
   Add a constrained, read-only execution path for translator-generated
   reasoning queries.
5. src/back/core/reasoning/swrl/SWRLEngine.py
   Route Neo4j inference queries through the constrained reasoning executor.
6. tests/units/simulation/test_simulation_runner_api.py and
   tests/units/reasoning/test_swrl_flat_cypher_translator.py
   Cover supported backend selection and Cypher output for the
   Customer-to-Contract-to-Meter rule.
7. README.md and docs/user-guide.md
   Document Delta and Neo4j simulation availability and sandbox isolation.

